# ------------------------------------------------------------------ pilot 1
"""Drive Like a Local, Track C pilot 1: the phantom jam. 9:16, 30 fps, 996 frames (33.2 s), no voice.

Set: a closed one-lane test ring (360 m lane centre line, radius 57.3 m) in October farmland, built with the
world.py materials (asphalt with wheel tracks, 0.25 m edge lines, Bankett, Leitpfosten Zeichen 620 on both sides,
left posts with two round reflectors), flora.py trees, village houses and wind turbines from world.py, HDRI sky.
22 cars (vehicles.py) drive the IDM simulation of trackc/phantom_sim.py frame by frame: one driver taps the brakes,
the jam forms and travels backwards while every car drives forwards. A red band on the road marks the standing jam,
roof chips show each car's speed class (green, amber, red), two arrows show "cars forwards, jam backwards".
Shots and timings: trackc/tc01_plan.py (the plan is shared with the captions and the sound).

Run: python tc01_phantom_jam.py OUTDIR --frames 1-996 --res 720 --samples 16 --assets ASSETS [--stills 60,300]
The look-dev copy lookdev/ld_trackc.py is this file with the simulation data embedded (trackc/bundle.py).
"""
